post_install() {
    cat <<EOF

==> Wavelog Installation Notes
==> ============================
1. DATABASE SETUP
   Create Wavelog database and users in MySQL/MariaDB
2. WEB SERVER CONFIGURATION
   Examples:
   /var/lib/wavelog/config/apache.example.conf
   /var/lib/wavelog/config/nginx.example.conf
3. PHP EXTENSIONS
   REQUIRED extensions:
   Edit /etc/php/php.ini and uncomment:
     extension=mysqli
     extension=gd
     extension=zip
   OPTIONAL caching extensions (for better performance):
   $ sudo nano /etc/php/conf.d/igbinary.ini  # Uncomment: extension=igbinary.so
   $ sudo nano /etc/php/conf.d/redis.ini     # Uncomment: extension=redis
   $ sudo nano /etc/php/conf.d/apcu.ini      # Uncomment: extension=apcu.so
   Restart web server after enabling extensions:
   $ sudo systemctl restart httpd      # Apache
   $ sudo systemctl restart php-fpm    # Nginx
5. WEB-BASED INSTALLATION
   Open your browser and navigate to: http://localhost/wavelog
   Follow the Wavelog installer.
EOF
}

